  "editorial": "operator.itemgetter(index) is the key. It raises if a row is short, which is what you want: a missing column is a bad table, not a value to drop. Checking first returns a clean error string instead of a traceback.",
  "reference_solution": "def solve(rows, index):\n    if index < 0 or any(len(row) <= index for row in rows):\n        return \"error\"\n    ordered = sorted(rows, key=lambda row: row[index])\n    return [list(row) for row in ordered]\n"
}
